<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Asiatic Vespers</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">88 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> · Also known as Ephesian Vespers</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Asiatic Vespers was the massacre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> and Italians in the province of Asia and neighbouring regions ordered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mithridates-vi-of-pontus">Mithridates VI of Pontus</a> in 88 BCE, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-mithridatic-war">First Mithridatic War</a>. Ancient writers put the number of dead at 80,000 or more. Many Greek cities, resentful of Roman tax-farmers and moneylenders, carried out the order, and the massacre made the war a bitter struggle.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/asiatic-vespers.jpg" alt="Asiatic Vespers" width="320" height="253" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ilya Yakubovich · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1stMithritadicwar89BC.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
